      "notes": "The full source EOS adds a specialized thermal term built from a Gaussian heat-capacity function and a volume-dependent Gruneisen parameter. That thermal form is not currently represented by the eosmat schema, so this record deliberately stores only the explicitly defined, directly executable 2500 K BM4 reference isotherm. The exact 40-state liquid selection is bundled. The paper derives Cv from energy-temperature slopes and gamma from pressure-energy slopes before fitting their volume functions; the supporting information supplies those observations only as raster plots, whose regression-line slopes are now digitized in a separate dataset. The digitization closely recovers the published Cv function but cannot recover the authors' unknown relative weighting for the gamma function. Consequently, subtracting either rounded published or digitized thermal coefficients from Table 1 and freely fitting four BM4 coefficients remains an ill-conditioned sensitivity experiment, not a reproduction of the source regression.",
